  "id": "Barking_&_Dagenham-26_00302_FULL",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Conversion of the existing dwelling into 3x flats (1x 2- bed, 1x 1- bed and 1x studio) with associated external amenity area, car parking and cycle and refuse storage",
  "development_type": "Minor all other minor developments",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a good quality family-sized dwellinghouse. This would be detrimental to the borough&#39;s stock of these type of dwellings, the identified local need for which is set out in the Development Plan and supporting evidence. The harm caused by way of a reduction in the borough&#39;s supply of this type of dwellinghouse significantly and demonstrably outweighs the benefits of the proposed flats.&nbsp;As such, the proposal would conflict with the following policies which seek to ensure that the borough&#39;s housing supply meets the needs of its residents:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies D6, H1, H2, H9 and&nbsp;H10 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SPDG 1,&nbsp;SP3 and DMH5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)",
    "The proposed development would fail to provide an adequate quality of accommodation for future occupiers. In particular, the proposed units would be fail to provide sufficient internal amenity space resultant of the splitting of the existing dwelling house. It would have an awkward arrangement. Poor external amenity is proposed. The proposal would therefore be harmful to the living conditions of future occupiers, contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals provide a high standard of amenity:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policies&nbsp;D6 and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMSI3&nbsp;of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)"
  ],
